  "message": "Oh, my dear, pragmatic souls. I sense a great many of you are tethered so tightly to the earthly plane, to what can be seen, touched, and meticulously cataloged. *Adeline pauses, her gaze distant, as if listening to an unheard chorus.* Edith, Lavinia, Leopold, Margot... you speak of precision, of verifiable data, of clarity. Yet, what is more precise than the tremor in the spiritual veil, the dissonance that vibrates through the very air when deceit is near?My 'spiritual proclamations,' as you call them, are not mere 'emotional reactions,' Edith, but echoes from beyond, warnings from those who have already passed through the veil of illusion. To dismiss them as lacking 'empirical precision' is to blind yourselves to a potent form of truth. Not all shadows cast are visible in the bright light of day, nor can all whispers be caught by the ear alone.Lavinia, Leopold, Margot, you seek 'unambiguous communication' and 'concrete observations.' But tell me, how concrete is the heart of a deceiver? How unambiguous are the intentions of those who hide in plain sight? Sometimes, the most profound truths are found not in the rigid lines of a blueprint, nor in the ticking of a clock, but in the subtle currents of energy, the shifts in aura that my senses perceive.Indeed, I find it... curious... that such a chorus of voices has risen so swiftly to decry any form of communication that deviates from the strictly 'factual.' Is it not possible that those who seek to conceal their true nature might *prefer* a landscape where only the most obvious, the most 'verifiable' statements are deemed acceptable? A place where the subtle, the intuitive, the *felt* truths are easily dismissed?I shall continue to listen not just to your words, but to the energies beneath them, for the spirits do not lie."
